hexagon: model the VTCM and layout limits of the DSP kernels in supports_op
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Findings dsp-vtcm-binary, dsp-vtcm-glu, dsp-vtcm-softmax, dsp-vtcm-concat,
dsp-vtcm-rows, dsp-vtcm-gdn, dsp-unary-block0, dsp-hmx-align and
dsp-cpy-layout of fuzz-hexhost, task #159. For each of these ops the host
accepted an op in supports_op that the DSP kernel then refuses, or does
incorrectly. Thus the op does not go to the CPU. On the 8 MB VTCM of the v79
the shapes of Qwen3.5 are in the limits. Task #62 ships one APK for chips
with a smaller VTCM, and there these limits apply.

The host now models each check of the DSP. The comments give the file and
the lines of the kernel:

- The binary ops: each thread holds two rows of src0 and of dst in VTCM (and
  of src1 for the same shape), and a broadcast row of src1 stays in VTCM
  one time.
- The GLU ops: each thread holds one row of src0, src1 and dst.
- SOFT_MAX: each thread holds two scratch pads of src0 and one of dst, of 4
  rows each.
- CONCAT: the 2D path with a transposed src1 holds blocks of rows for each
  thread.
- GET_ROWS (with no DMA) and SET_ROWS: the VTCM layout of the kernel params.
- GATED_DELTA_NET: each thread holds two state blocks of S_v x S_v floats.
- The unary ops: the VTCM layout of the kernel params, and a layout with no
  row of src0 in VTCM (BLOCK 0). The fusion of RMS_NORM and MUL does the
  same check.
- The HMX matmul: the addresses of src1 and dst, and the batch strides, must
  be multiples of 128 bytes. Else the HVX path runs.
- CPY: the layout test of the DSP. There an element stride that is not the
  type size, or rows that overlap, count as transposed.

For three items the kernel did not refuse the op. This patch adds a check
that returns HTP_STATUS_VTCM_TOO_SMALL:

- get-rows-ops.c and set-rows-ops.c wrote their VTCM layout with no check of
  the reservation (dsp-vtcm-rows).
- gated-delta-net-ops.c had an assert only, and an assert is empty in the
  release library (dsp-vtcm-gdn).
- unary-ops.c returned OK with no output for BLOCK 0 (dsp-unary-block0).

Evidence (2026-09-23):
- The nine regression inputs of these items in tests/fuzz/hexhost/regress/
  kparams give the finding before this patch (the model of the DSP kernels
  in the fake DSP of fuzz-hexhost) in the test runs of the campaign, debug
  and release. With the five patches of fuzz-hexhost they give no finding in
  the asan build, debug and release.
- The kparams fuzzer with the conditions of tasks #155 and #159 on ran 6
  times for 100 s with the patches: no finding.
- The supports_op decision of each op of the Qwen3.5 graphs is the same
  before and after, with the values of the v79 (x86, the real-graph tool of
  fuzz-hexhost with the fake DSP). The dumps of the 2B decode (112
  decisions), the 2B prefill (147), the 4B decode (118) and the 4B prefill
  (155) have no difference, and each op stays on HTP0. The count of each op
  kind of each graph is the same.
- The DSP libraries for v73, v75, v79 and v81 build with this patch. The
  kernel lab (tools/htp-lab) has no target that runs these checks. Task #123
  holds the missing lab targets.
- The phone check of the five patches of fuzz-hexhost together (OnePlus 13,
  the 2B Q8_0 on HTP0, thermal status 0, cpu7 cap 4.32 GHz, battery 27.6 to
  27.7 °C, MemAvailable 8.9 to 9.5 GB):
  - test-backend-ops on HTP0: GATED_DELTA_NET and SSM_CONV (101 cases),
    CONCAT CPY GET_ROWS SET_ROWS (267 cases), the binary ops with GLU and
    SOFT_MAX (385 cases), NORM RMS_NORM SCALE (127 cases). Each group passes
    before and after.
  - llama-bench tg32 -r 3 after one warmup at 23.76 t/s: before 23.56 ±
    0.10, after 23.59 ± 0.27, before 23.63 ± 0.13, after 23.57 ± 0.11 t/s.
  - llama-speculative-simple with the MTP draft of depth 4, temperature 0,
    64 tokens: before 23.589 and 23.685 t/s, after 24.076 and 24.029 t/s.
    Each run accepts 44 drafts (52.381 %), and the four runs give the same
    text.

Measurement: the host instructions for each decode token of the 4B Q8_0
graph (x86, the real-graph tool with the fake DSP, perf stat, with
GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE=0): 3,709,475 before this patch and 3,730,072 after
(+0.56 %). The tg32 of the phone check does not change.

